    cuda_gpu_gated_spec_defects_2026-08-09, 1, "2026-11-10 status fixing->open: stale sweep claim, no lane active; reopened for P2 burn-down"
    cuda_gpu_gated_spec_defects_2026-08-09, 2, "2026-11-26 enumeration on NVIDIA GB10 (aarch64, cc 12.1, driver 580.173.02) with SIMPLE_CUDA_TEST=1. Item 0 harness trap: no longer reproduces (one example now reports every failing assertion, e.g. 'expected 700 to equal 0' and 'expected -700 to equal 0' together). Items 1-2: gpu_ptx_gen_spec 81/81 after correcting the stale PTX ISA header expectation 7.8 -> 8.0 (ptx_builder PTX_ISA_VERSION). Item 3: feature/usage/cuda_spec 5/5 (compute capability already dlopen-backed); ctx_destroy, memcpy_dtod, module_load and get_error_string now dispatch through CudaFns."
    cuda_gpu_gated_spec_defects_2026-08-09, 3, "Item 3 red->green: cuda_interpreter_driver_shims_live_spec with seed /home/yoon/.cache/cargo-target-wr-seed1126b/release/simple fails 4/4 (48 ctx creates, 0 destroyed; dtod -3; module_load -2 once contexts leak; error names 'CUDA support disabled'); with rebuilt seed /home/yoon/.cache/cargo-target-claude-cudagated-1126/release/simple (sha256 f715eaa1f174b0b2..) passes 5/5 incl. device dtod and file-loaded kernel words equal to host values. New defect fixed in the same change: CudaSession.init kept a negative cuCtxCreate status (-2) as a valid ctx (red: status_ok=true ctx=-2 valid=true, 2 runs)."
    cuda_gpu_gated_spec_defects_2026-08-09, 4, "Item 4: 4.1/4.4 fixed earlier; 4.2 build rule now defaults CC to clang (plain cc is gcc here); 4.3 intermittent (Q15 spec 4/7 passes) -> simple_audio_cuda_q15_intermittent_device_failure_2026_11_26. Remainder split: cuda_interpreter_f64_compute_ops_sentinel_2026_11_26, cuda_runtime_not_cuda_stubs_no_dlopen_2026_11_26, test_feature_gpu_ptx_gen_spec_stale_duplicate_2026_11_26. Perf: cuda_compiler_ptx_live_spec base vs fix seed, 3 alternated rounds, 6.50/6.10/6.85 s vs 6.14/6.00/6.88 s, RSS equal."
    cuda_gpu_gated_spec_defects_2026-08-09, 5, "Review follow-up: rt_cuda_ctx_destroy refuses ctx <= 0 (a failed-create CUresult is never a handle); crypto_accel CudaSession had the same == 0 check and now uses <= 0. Exhaustion example moved to cuda_session_ctx_exhaustion_live_spec behind SIMPLE_CUDA_TEST. Seed /home/yoon/.cache/cargo-target-claude-cudagated-1126/release/simple sha256 8aa5a38eb1db4420..: shims 5/5, exhaustion 1/1; seed cargo-target-wr-seed1126b: 0/5 and 0/1. Census of gpu.rs interpreter shims: 48 total, 37 call get_cuda_dl directly, 4 delegate to dlopen siblings (module_load_data_array, memcpy_htod_array, launch_kernel_name_array, event_elapsed_ns), 7 rt_cuda_f64_* remain -3 (split shard)."
    cuda_gpu_gated_spec_defects_2026-08-09, 6, "Fable review follow-up: the cuda-feature runtime rt_cuda_ctx_destroy (cuda_runtime.rs) also refuses ctx <= 0; cargo test -p simple-runtime --features cuda ctx_destroy_refuses_failed_create_status SIGSEGVs inside cuCtxDestroy_v2(-2) without the guard and passes with it. The 512-context exhaustion spec is replaced by a deterministic unit example on cuda_session_ctx_failure_status (cuda_session_contract_spec 11/11): CudaFfi is a concrete class, so its ctx_create seam cannot be faked, and it already clamps a negative create to 0. cuda_interpreter_driver_shims_live_spec is gated on SIMPLE_CUDA_TEST (5/5 gated, 1/1 skip otherwise)."

